# A database of meaning-specific age-of-acquisition ratings for 562 Mandarin Chinese disyllabic homonyms

## Overview

This repository provides data, analysis code, and reproducible outputs for meaning-level Age of Acquisition (AoA) norming in Chinese homonyms. The project is designed for research use, with explicit quality-control procedures, mixed-effects modeling, and reliability/validity checks.

The analyses are implemented in a single reproducible workflow:

- [code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.Rmd](code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.Rmd): full analysis pipeline
- [code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.md](code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.md): rendered report

Additional project documentation:

- [Supplementary Materials.pdf](Supplementary%20Materials.pdf): additional methodological details

## Study Components

### Experiment 1

- Focus: AoA rating patterns by lexical type (homonym, polyseme, monoseme)
- Processing: RT-based data screening and outlier handling
- Modeling: linear mixed-effects models for rating scores and rating latency

### Experiment 2

- Focus: meaning-level norming and internal reliability
- Processing: anchor-based quality checks and participant screening
- Reliability: split-half reliability with Spearman-Brown correction
- Modeling: AoA-latency relationships at the trial level

### Validation Analyses

- Convergent validity against published word-level AoA norms
- Predictive validity in a homonym disambiguation dataset

## Repository Layout

### Analysis code

- [code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.Rmd](code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.Rmd): source analysis notebook
- [code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.md](code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.md): knitted markdown output
- [code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis_files/figure-gfm](code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis_files/figure-gfm): generated figures

### Data files

- [data/Exp1rating_HPM_data.csv](data/Exp1rating_HPM_data.csv): Experiment 1 trial-level responses
- [data/Exp1rating_HPM_stimuli.csv](data/Exp1rating_HPM_stimuli.csv): Experiment 1 stimulus metadata
- [data/Exp2rating_homonym_data.csv](data/Exp2rating_homonym_data.csv): Experiment 2 trial-level responses
- [data/Exp2rating_homonym_stimuli.csv](data/Exp2rating_homonym_stimuli.csv): Experiment 2 stimulus metadata
- [data/anchor_trials_in_both_experiments.csv](data/anchor_trials_in_both_experiments.csv): anchor items rated in both experiments
- [data/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_norms.csv](data/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_norms.csv): meaning-level AoA norms
- [data/Homonym disambiguation judgments_(Xie et al., 2025).csv](data/Homonym%20disambiguation%20judgments_(Xie%20et%20al.,%202025).csv): external behavioral dataset for predictive-validity analyses

### Supplementary document

- [Supplementary Materials.pdf](Supplementary%20Materials.pdf): 11-page supplementary materials file included at the repository root

## Reproducibility

### Software

- R (recommended: 4.2 or higher)
- RStudio (optional)

### Main R packages

- tidyverse (dplyr, tidyr, readr, stringr, purrr)
- ggplot2, ggpubr, ggsci, ggstatsplot, patchwork
- lme4, lmerTest, emmeans, rstatix, ez
- readxl, arrow, xtable

### Execution steps

1. Clone the repository.
2. Open [code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.Rmd](code/Chinese_homonym_meaning_level_AoA_analysis.Rmd).
3. Set working directory to repository root (or adjust paths in the script).
4. Install/load required R packages.
5. Knit the R Markdown document to reproduce tables and figures.

## Citation and Use

If you use these data or analyses, please cite the associated manuscript or project output by the repository authors. The repository also includes [Supplementary Materials.pdf](Supplementary%20Materials.pdf) for the accompanying supplementary documentation.

